\sigma^2 = \frac{1}{9} [225 + 180 + 180 + 189 + 115 + 64 + 180 + 280 + 100 + 144]
\end{equation}

\begin{equation}
\sigma^2 = \frac{1}{9} [385]
\end{equation}

The sample variance is 385. This means that the values in the sample are more spread out than the mean would suggest.

